# Backend setup (Windows PowerShell)

Run commands from this directory:

```powershell
.\venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pip install -r requirements.txt
.\venv\Scripts\python.exe -m uvicorn main:app --reload --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000
```

Configure local credentials in `.env` before starting the server. Do not commit
that file. PostgreSQL must be running and its credentials must match the values
in `.env`.

- Swagger UI: http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs
- ReDoc: http://127.0.0.1:8000/redoc
- Health check: http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/health
- Application log: `logs/system.log`

The health check runs `SELECT 1`; it returns HTTP 503 when PostgreSQL is
unavailable. The backend does not create or modify database tables.
.\venv\Scripts\python.exe -m utils.seed_roles
.\venv\Scripts\uvicorn.exe main:app --reload